1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,500
But it's high! This shot went astray!

2
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:04,710
Ah, is it not a goal?

3
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:08,050
What!?

4
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:11,220
No, this is a Drive Shot!

5
00:00:11,510 --> 00:00:14,430
Not only did he strike the ball a moment before Schneider...

6
00:00:14,510 --> 00:00:17,560
...he also put spin on it.

7
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:22,980
This is the shot of the genius footballer Ozora Tsubasa, the Flying Scissor Drive.

8
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:27,230
Is the referee about to blow the whistle?

9
00:00:27,480 --> 00:00:32,240
Tsubasa goes to strike the spinning ball!

10
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:41,870
Tsubasa jumps!

11
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:43,830
This...

12
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:48,500
The final shot!

13
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:52,380
Tsubasa executes a ground-level overhead kick!

14
00:00:52,550 --> 00:00:53,380
I got it!

15
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:58,100
But Germany's goalkeeper Müller reacts and dives in its direction.

16
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:01,020
What!?

17
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:04,650
The ball rises and goes into the air!

18
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:08,440
It's- It's in the goal!

19
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:13,320
And the final whistle declares the end of the game.

20
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:17,580
The Japanese youth win! They did it!

21
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:21,700
Japan has become the world champion!

22
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:26,920
We did it!

23
00:01:27,210 --> 00:01:32,880
The entire Japan team runs toward their champion, captain Tsubasa.

24
00:01:32,970 --> 00:01:35,340
Even the substitutes.

25
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:38,390
See? I told you.

26
00:01:38,470 --> 00:01:42,020
Tsubasa always finds a way, you little rascal!

27
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:43,560
Ishizaki.

28
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:44,690
Ishizaki.

29
00:01:45,190 --> 00:01:47,520
No, it was thanks to you all.

30
00:01:47,610 --> 00:01:50,150
We succeeded thanks to your hard work.

31
00:01:50,650 --> 00:01:52,690
We won!

32
00:01:55,110 --> 00:01:58,530
We became number one, and our dream has come true.

33
00:01:58,870 --> 00:02:04,080
Thank God. Thank you so much for football.

34
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:21,260
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

35
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:41,460
Episode 36
A Vow to the Sky

36
00:03:42,250 --> 00:03:43,540
Tears are flowing.

37
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:46,380
What a magnificent moment for the Japanese youth.

38
00:03:46,590 --> 00:03:49,260
Every athlete is overwhelmed with emotion.

39
00:03:49,670 --> 00:03:54,430
For the first time, Japan is incredibly becoming number one in the world!

40
00:03:55,180 --> 00:03:58,430
Look at the champions of the National Youth Tournament in France!

41
00:04:01,890 --> 00:04:03,190
For the first time in history...

42
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:07,190
...Japanese football has been magnificently recognized as the world champion.

43
00:04:13,070 --> 00:04:15,160
Great save, Wakabayashi.

44
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:16,200
Yes.

45
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:29,550
Congratulations, Japan team!

46
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:32,220
Schneider!

47
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:38,180
Finally, after their heated battle...

48
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:41,720
...the two captains shake hands on the field.

49
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:44,230
No one can deny it.

50
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:46,690
You are number one.

51
00:04:49,190 --> 00:04:54,030
But this time, I want to exchange our armbands.

52
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:57,370
Because...

53
00:04:58,490 --> 00:05:01,330
...our battle has only just begun.

54
00:05:02,540 --> 00:05:03,450
Yes.

55
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:05,420
I want to fight you again.

56
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:07,250
And on an even bigger stage.

57
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:09,590
Yes, me too.

58
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:11,300
Only next time I won't lose.

59
00:05:13,010 --> 00:05:13,840
Okay.

60
00:05:20,890 --> 00:05:24,310
Wakabayashi, when I become a professional, I'll make up for this.

61
00:05:24,810 --> 00:05:25,890
Yes.

62
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:28,770
But I also have no intention of losing.

63
00:05:33,690 --> 00:05:34,940
And the official result has been announced.

64
00:05:35,030 --> 00:05:41,030
The Japanese youth are the champions, and the German youth are the runners-up.

65
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:47,120
And first, to the German players...

66
00:05:47,210 --> 00:05:49,130
...the silver medals are being presented.

67
00:05:55,130 --> 00:05:58,890
The first medal goes to Captain Karl Heinz Schneider.

68
00:06:02,390 --> 00:06:07,230
With his 12 goals, he earned the title of top scorer of this tournament.

69
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:10,560
Big brother.

70
00:06:10,650 --> 00:06:11,940
Karl!

71
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:14,940
Well done, Karl.

72
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:30,880
We fought fairly and used all our strength.

73
00:06:31,290 --> 00:06:33,000
There's nothing to be ashamed of.

74
00:06:34,340 --> 00:06:37,170
So, let's applaud Japan.

75
00:06:44,010 --> 00:06:49,600
The German youth send Japan to the podium with applause.

76
00:06:58,780 --> 00:07:04,530
And now, each player of the Japan team is receiving a gold medal.

77
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:07,580
First is Captain Tsubasa.

78
00:07:09,330 --> 00:07:13,080
He held the team together both as a playmaker and as captain.

79
00:07:13,170 --> 00:07:14,630
And guided them all the way.

80
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:20,050
He is undoubtedly the key player of the Japanese youth.

81
00:07:20,130 --> 00:07:23,140
Japan Team Won! Congratulations, Japanese Youth!

82
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:23,140
His final victorious strike, without a doubt...

83
00:07:23,510 --> 00:07:26,260
...will remain in memories for years to come.

84
00:07:28,180 --> 00:07:33,900
And in this order, Tsubasa is being presented with the Most Valuable Player award.

85
00:07:34,150 --> 00:07:37,730
This young Japanese footballer, now the pride of the world...

86
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:39,150
...Ozora Tsubasa!

87
00:07:46,370 --> 00:07:49,160
Tsubasa may be the playmaker...

88
00:07:49,370 --> 00:07:53,170
...but Hyuga is Japan's best forward.

89
00:07:54,580 --> 00:07:58,960
He scored 5 goals and became the team's main goal scorer.

90
00:07:59,050 --> 00:08:01,590
Japan Team Won! Congratulations, Japanese Youth!

91
00:07:59,510 --> 00:08:02,430
Kojiro Hyuga is a true wild tiger.

92
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:07,640
Next...

93
00:08:08,310 --> 00:08:10,310
Tsubasa's talented partner...

94
00:08:10,390 --> 00:08:12,390
Japan Team Won! Congratulations, Japanese Youth!

95
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:13,480
...and another pillar of Japan's midfield.

96
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:18,360
He undoubtedly deserves the title of the Golden Duo.

97
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:22,110
He lives in France. He is Taro Misaki.

98
00:08:25,870 --> 00:08:29,620
Next is the goalkeeper of this final match, Genzo Wakabayashi.

99
00:08:30,450 --> 00:08:33,120
He stepped in for the injured Wakashimazu.

100
00:08:33,620 --> 00:08:36,750
And magnificently guarded Japan's goal.

101
00:08:37,340 --> 00:08:42,300
It's no surprise his nickname is "Super Goalkeeper".

102
00:08:43,170 --> 00:08:45,090
Now the defensive line.

103
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:46,640
First is Matsuyama.

104
00:08:47,890 --> 00:08:49,890
He used to be a midfielder.

105
00:08:49,970 --> 00:08:53,560
But he performed well in the defensive midfielder role.

106
00:08:52,310 --> 00:08:54,060
Japan Team Won! Congratulations, Japanese Youth!

107
00:08:54,310 --> 00:08:57,810
Training in snowy lands, he was no less than his opponents.

108
00:08:58,400 --> 00:09:00,020
Next on defense is Soda.

109
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:04,400
Despite getting a yellow card against France, he played in the final.

110
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:07,780
And next is Jito.

111
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:14,960
He was truly the guardian god of the Japan team.

112
00:09:15,790 --> 00:09:20,000
And next is Izawa, who replaced Ishizaki in the final minutes.

113
00:09:20,420 --> 00:09:24,340
He filled Ishizaki's place well.

114
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:27,090
Next, the three young players.

115
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:29,260
The first is the skilled youngster Sawada.

116
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:32,140
He was Hyuga's partner from Toho Academy.

117
00:09:32,220 --> 00:09:36,060
Here in France, they were also a wonderful substitute combination.

118
00:09:43,230 --> 00:09:45,700
Next is forward Nitta.

119
00:09:46,280 --> 00:09:49,910
He showed us the evolution of his Falcon Shot.

120
00:09:50,830 --> 00:09:52,740
And finally, midfielder Sano.

121
00:09:53,330 --> 00:09:56,370
Together, they are three true warriors.

122
00:09:58,210 --> 00:10:00,710
And of course, goalkeeper Wakashimazu.

123
00:10:01,380 --> 00:10:04,130
He may have given up his place in the final to Wakabayashi...

124
00:10:04,630 --> 00:10:09,090
...but in the semifinal, he guarded Japan's goal at the cost of his life.

125
00:10:10,470 --> 00:10:12,010
And here are the Tachibana Brothers.

126
00:10:12,100 --> 00:10:14,520
They didn't let their injuries stop them from performing their Space Storm...

127
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:17,190
...and they deeply impressed us.

128
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:20,730
And Misugi.

129
00:10:20,860 --> 00:10:24,690
The extraordinary overhead kick he scored against Argentina's goal...

130
00:10:24,780 --> 00:10:26,400
...we will never forget.

131
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:32,200
And of course, Japan's brave player, Ishizaki.

132
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:38,370
He fought in this final with his special Face Block.

133
00:10:40,580 --> 00:10:42,170
Peace, peace.

134
00:10:42,250 --> 00:10:44,500
Japan Team Won! Congratulations, Japanese Youth!

135
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:44,500
I did it, Mom!

136
00:10:44,590 --> 00:10:46,840
- Do you see?
- My dear.

137
00:10:47,590 --> 00:10:52,350
Next is forward Sorimachi, who played in 2 matches in this tournament.

138
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:57,430
Morisaki, Takasugi, Taki, and Kizugi.

139
00:10:57,640 --> 00:11:00,560
They may not have been able to play in this tournament...

140
00:11:00,650 --> 00:11:03,360
...but from the bench, they wholeheartedly supported the 11 players on the field.

141
00:11:03,980 --> 00:11:07,400
Their support is part of this victory.

142
00:11:07,610 --> 00:11:13,530
The Japan team's victory is truly the product of teamwork.

143
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:18,960
And finally, the president of the tournament, Mr. Michel Leboeuf...

144
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:21,120
...is presenting the winners' cup.

145
00:11:22,670 --> 00:11:25,840
And of course, the recipient is Captain Tsubasa.

146
00:11:29,550 --> 00:11:31,470
We did it!

147
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:38,310
We are number one!

148
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:41,100
A true victory!

149
00:11:41,190 --> 00:11:47,480
The Japanese youth, Under-15 World Champions!

